Description: Command line options for every setting; no config file without -f
 Every minidlna.conf option can now be given on the command line as
 --name=value or --name value ('-' and '_' interchangeable). Command line
 values are applied after the config file so they win; the first command
 line value of media_dir, album_art_names or network_interface replaces the
 file's list. Unknown options print the usage and exit.
 .
 A configuration file is only read when given with -f, as the init scripts
 do. Without -f, built-in defaults and command line options apply and
 minidlnad serves the current directory ($PWD, or getcwd() if $PWD is
 stale) as the invoking user. album_art_names now defaults to the list in
 the shipped minidlna.conf instead of being empty.
 .
 wide_links now defaults to yes, and every yes/no option can be switched
 both ways so a command line value can override the file. Option values may
 be up to PATH_MAX long (was 200 bytes).
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
